('d4b454f0-eda6-4a35-b78b-72c04484f2cc', 'd585435a-10fa-4be9-91af-5303a4204ef8', 'pyq', 'Hindi- October 2025', 'Practice PYQs and Ace your Endsems.', '', 2025, 'https://h36y6svq.us-east.insforge.app/api/storage/buckets/cue-pyqs/objects/d585435a-10fa-4be9-91af-5303a4204ef8%2F2025%2Fa3d40074-6d7d-4814-b472-729b40020dea-elementary-hindi-2025.pdf?v=a85ebd40a288e9824f8e95ec8dbb93c5', 'd585435a-10fa-4be9-91af-5303a4204ef8/2025/a3d40074-6d7d-4814-b472-729b40020dea-elementary-hindi-2025.pdf', 1, true, 'Regular Examination', 'Elementary_Hindi_2025.pdf', 29133, 'a3d40074-6d7d-4814-b472-729b40020dea', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-17 12:15:55.36793+00', '2026-09-17 12:27:45.712098+00'),
('515f261c-d752-4fa9-8079-aecac6407e5a', '4942b243-3eda-4100-9200-942a29e98d11', 'flashcard', 'IPO numerical 2: Book Building: cut-off price.', 'Priority: Tier 2 | PYQ Connection: Syllabus (Book Building Process)', 'Question: A company offers 12,00,000 shares in a price band of ₹100–110. Bids received are shown below. Find the cut-off price.

Price (₹) | Bids at price | Cumulative demand (at or above that price)
110 | 2,00,000 | 2,00,000
108 | 3,00,000 | 5,00,000
106 | 4,00,000 | 9,00,000
104 | 5,00,000 | 14,00,000
102 | 3,00,000 | 17,00,000
100 | 3,00,000 | 20,00,000

Concept: Cut-off price = the highest price at which cumulative demand is at least equal to the issue size.

Steps:

Build the cumulative demand column, from the highest price downwards.
At ₹106, cumulative demand = 9,00,000, which is below 12,00,000 (not enough).
At ₹104, cumulative demand = 14,00,000, which is above 12,00,000 ✓.

Final answer: Cut-off price = ₹104.

Subscription at ₹104 = 14,00,000 ÷ 12,00,000 = 1.17 times.
Proceeds = 12,00,000 × 104 = ₹12,48,00,000.
Bidders at ₹102 and ₹100 get nothing. Bidders at ₹104 and above pay ₹104 (uniform price). Allotment ratio = 12 ÷ 14 ≈ 85.7%.

Exam tip: Never use the total demand at the floor price (20,00,000) to decide the cut-off.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 36, true, 'University Exam', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'adc29a92-1496-4a49-9e94-09ce4fd912da', 'bd81773e-1a5e-4ef0-8417-167ad3e3dad3', '{"blocks": [{"id": "edm-u2-c36-q-1", "text": "IPO numerical 2: Book Building: cut-off price.", "type": "text", "style": "paragraph"}], "version": 1}'::jsonb, '{"blocks": [{"id": "edm-u2-c36-a-1", "text": "Question: A company offers 12,00,000 shares in a price band of ₹100–110. Bids received are shown below. Find the cut-off price.", "type": "text", "style": "paragraph"}, {"id": "edm-u2-c36-a-2", "rows": [["Price (₹)", "Bids at price", "Cumulative demand (at or above that price)"], ["110", "2,00,000", "2,00,000"], ["108", "3,00,000", "5,00,000"], ["106", "4,00,000", "9,00,000"], ["104", "5,00,000", "14,00,000"], ["102", "3,00,000", "17,00,000"], ["100", "3,00,000", "20,00,000"]], "type": "table"}, {"id": "edm-u2-c36-a-3", "text": "Concept: Cut-off price = the highest price at which cumulative demand is at least equal to the issue size.", "type": "text", "style": "paragraph"}, {"id": "edm-u2-c36-a-4", "bold": true, "text": "Steps:", "type": "text", "style": "heading"}, {"id": "edm-u2-c36-a-5", "type": "numberList", "items": ["Build the cumulative demand column, from the highest price downwards.", "At ₹106, cumulative demand = 9,00,000, which is below 12,00,000 (not enough).", "At ₹104, cumulative demand = 14,00,000, which is above 12,00,000 ✓."]}, {"id": "edm-u2-c36-a-6", "text": "Final answer: Cut-off price = ₹104.", "type": "text", "style": "paragraph"}, {"id": "edm-u2-c36-a-7", "type": "bulletList", "items": ["Subscription at ₹104 = 14,00,000 ÷ 12,00,000 = 1.17 times.", "Proceeds = 12,00,000 × 104 = ₹12,48,00,000.", "Bidders at ₹102 and ₹100 get nothing. Bidders at ₹104 and above pay ₹104 (uniform price). Allotment ratio = 12 ÷ 14 ≈ 85.7%."]}, {"id": "edm-u2-c36-a-8", "text": "Exam tip: Never use the total demand at the floor price (20,00,000) to decide the cut-off.", "type": "text", "style": "paragraph"}], "version": 1}'::jsonb, '2026-09-20 18:07:19.465361+00', '2026-09-20 18:07:19.465361+00'),
('e73cf663-e185-4eea-a62a-b59826dce7f0', '5c93c785-bc3e-4489-969c-9ec5f21c174a', 'syllabus_unit', 'Macro Economics Issues and Framework', '', '● Scope and Importance of Macro Economics
